# Agent Skills format

Each canonical skill lives at `skills/<name>/SKILL.md`. The directory name must
match the frontmatter `name`. Keep portable workflow rules in the core and
repository-specific paths and conventions in a sibling `overlay.md`.

Use this source shape:

```text
skills/
  <skill-name>/
    SKILL.md
    <detail>.md
    assets/
    references/
    scripts/
```

Start `SKILL.md` with:

```yaml
---
name: skill-name
description: What the skill does and the literal requests that should invoke it.
license: MIT
metadata:
  portability: portable
  applicability: universal
  binding: optional-overlay
  risk: advisory
  maturity: canary
  requires: none
  related: none
---
```

`name` uses lowercase letters, digits, and hyphens and matches its directory.
The description is the routing surface. `requires` names hard dependencies;
`related` names optional handoffs. Relationship names must resolve and the
required graph must remain acyclic.

An overlay-aware portable core reads `overlay.md` when present. Its overlay
starts with the matching core and immutable review pin:

```yaml
---
core: skill-name
core-pin: v1.2.3
---
```

Vendored runtime copies under `.agents/skills/` are immutable upstream mirrors.
Record local bindings in overlays and preserve source repository, revision,
pin, path, and tree-SHA provenance.

Run `./tools/Validate-Repository.ps1` and `Invoke-Pester ./tests` when those
tools are present. Regenerate a source catalog with
`./tools/Update-SkillCatalog.ps1 -Apply`.
